hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-11 = unlines (cons "The boundary where joined things meet is where hyperactivity puts logic: logical compatibility at every expressed boundary. *Compatible* is *com* + *pati*, to suffer together. *Pati* is the Latin of *passion* and *patient*, and its Greek counterpart *pathos* is inside *empathy*. Compatibility, at the root, is co-suffering. So the phrase says there is co-suffering at every boundary that gets expressed: wherever two systems meet, each takes the other's state into itself. A type check at a boundary is a formal empathy: one side admits what the other is, exactly as it is." nil)
